{
  // SCRUM-89 — the DEPLOY config for the website half of the universal link.
  //
  // Why this file exists: Cloudflare's current "Connect to Git" flow for this
  // project is **Workers Builds**, whose deploy step runs `npx wrangler deploy`.
  // That command reads THIS file to learn what to publish. Without it there is
  // no Worker and no assets directory, so the deploy has nothing to ship and
  // `https://josspaperar.app/.well-known/assetlinks.json` never appears.
  //
  // Docs: developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/binding/
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",

  // ⚠️ MUST MATCH the Worker/project name you created in the Cloudflare
  // dashboard. If they differ you end up with TWO Workers and the domain points
  // at the empty one. Rename this line to match, or ask and it will be changed.
  "name": "josspaperar-links",

  // Per the Cloudflare docs: "Set this to today's date".
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-11",

  // Workers Logs. ⚠️ MEASURED 2026-10-11 — capture is PARTIAL and unreliable.
  //
  // The config below is correct and IS live (API-verified: `enabled: true`,
  // `redact_query_string: true`). What it CAPTURES is the problem.
  //
  // Over 6 hours of probing with known traffic — curl AND browser-like headers,
  // across the custom domain, the workers.dev host and a preview alias:
  //   · exactly 4 events captured, ALL from ONE browser visit to a PREVIEW
  //     hostname (`4c70b1d7…`) at 07:19Z;
  //   · NOTHING from the production deployment has been captured;
  //   · 0 `/join/*` requests captured, across three distinct probes;
  //   · 0 `.well-known/*` requests captured.
  //
  // CAUSE — an upstream, long-standing Cloudflare bug: requests served by the
  // **static-assets layer** do not reach Workers Logs or tail events.
  // cloudflare/workers-sdk#8724, "Static Assets is not compatible with Workers
  // Logs" — closed Apr 2025 as not-reproducible, then re-reported Oct 2025,
  // Feb 2026 and Jul 2026. A reproduction comment pins it: "Console logs work
  // UNTIL I add [assets] … directory", and "user workers with an assets binding
  // stopped showing up in tail events ENTIRELY".
  //
  // ⚠️ Every request here is served by that layer — `/.well-known/*` as an asset
  // and `/join/*` via `_redirects` — and this is an ASSETS-ONLY Worker
  // (`has_modules: false`), so there is no script invocation for a log to describe.
  //
  // ⚠️ WHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE INVITE CODE — after TWO overclaiming corrections:
  //  · THE MECHANISM IS REAL. A captured event's message is literally
  //    "GET https://<host><path>" — the FULL URL. So a captured `/join/{CODE}`
  //    WOULD put the code into log storage, against doc 07 §4.6.
  //  · WHETHER `/join/*` IS EVER SAMPLED IS UNKNOWN. None has been observed — but
  //    the sampler demonstrably drops almost everything, so that absence is WEAK
  //    evidence, not proof.
  //  ⚠️ THIS FILE WAS WRONG TWICE. It first warned that codes WOULD leak, then
  //  retracted that by saying nothing is logged at all. Both were overclaims, each
  //  built on a single measurement. The honest state is: REAL mechanism,
  //  UNQUANTIFIED exposure. Treat §4.6 as at odds with `invocation_logs: true`
  //  until the sampling behaviour is understood — the mitigation, if wanted, is
  //  `invocation_logs: false` (which costs all logs, there being no script here).
  //  · DIAGNOSTIC. Still unusable: you CANNOT reliably watch Apple's CDN or
  //    Android fetch the association files from here.
  //
  // Left enabled on purpose: it costs nothing, captures nothing, and begins working
  // by itself if Cloudflare fixes #8724 — or the day a Worker script is added.
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true,

    // Kept as hygiene rather than as protection: nothing here ever needs a query
    // string logged, and the custom-scheme fallback (`josspaperar://join?code=…`)
    // uses one. It would not have covered a code in the PATH anyway — and on the
    // evidence above, neither was ever needed.
    "redact_query_string": true,

    "logs": {
      "enabled": true,
      "invocation_logs": true,
      "persist": true
    }
  },

  // No `main` — this is an ASSETS-ONLY Worker (no script to run). Static files
  // are served directly, which is all the association files need.
  //
  // ⚠️ `./public/` is the docs' own example value: "The folder of static assets
  // to be served. For many frameworks, this is the ./public/, ./dist/, or
  // ./build/ folder."
  //
  // ⚠️ Do NOT add an `.assetsignore` listing `_redirects` / `_headers`. The
  // Cloudflare docs show that example for people who do NOT want those files
  // processed — the opposite of what we want. Workers parses them; they are
  // never served as static assets:
  //   "This file will not itself be served as a static asset, but will instead
  //    be parsed by Workers and its rules will be applied."
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public/"
  },

  // ⚠️ REQUIRED — without it EVERY PR's Cloudflare check FAILS.
  //
  // Cloudflare runs the Preview command (default `npx wrangler preview`) on every
  // NON-production branch — i.e. every PR. It refuses to run without this block:
  //
  //   ✘ [ERROR] Your Wrangler configuration is missing a `previews` block to run
  //     this command. Add the following to your configuration file:
  //       { "previews": {} }
  //
  // It may be EMPTY. Docs, verbatim: "The `previews` block is required, but it
  // can be empty if your Preview does not need separate settings." Assets,
  // compatibility settings, migrations and placement stay at the TOP LEVEL and
  // are deliberately not repeated here. Schema: `previews` → `PreviewsConfig`.
  //
  // ⚠️ THE TRAP THIS CLOSES: that failure surfaces ONLY as a GitHub check-run
  // named "Workers Builds: josspaperar-links". It is INVISIBLE to `npm run check`
  // and to `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — and an earlier pass on this repo duly
  // reported "CI green" while it was RED on two merged PRs (#34 and #35).
  // `check:links` now asserts this key, so the blind spot is closed rather than
  // remembered.
  "previews": {}
}
